Z||000017||Nikotek||05-14-2001||12:10 PM||||I too love my Fieros and would take them over almost any car,but here are a few words about the 300zxt I own. I have a 91' 300zx Turbo and one thing is for sure-acceleration is awesome. A ton of torque steer,you need to be ready for when the twin turbos kick in...the wheel can actually get away from you! Fit and finish on the interior is excellent-especially leather. My wife drives the 2000 Maxima which has an almost identical interior-Nissan does a very nice job. After 93,000 miles in 6 years,no electrical problems/mysteries ever. One fuel/air adjustment and regular maintenance. The only drawback is expensive parts and what I feel is high insurance($1400/year-I'm 30 and my wife is 27). If you have a chance at a later generation 300z don't hesitate-especially the turbo! The quality and comfort are top notch and performance is amazing! I only wish it was relatively inexpensive to modify one of my Fieros to match my 300's acceleration, comfort or rock solid feel I get at high speeds(144mph)cruising on these upstate Maryland roads...but that's not why I love my fiero or what it's about-as we all know.Hope this sheds a little light on the Z,keep trying to talk her into that Fiero!<P>------------------<BR>87' GT (355 Spyder)<BR>88' Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000018||Black88GT||05-14-2001||01:26 PM||||Yeah with Nissan you know you are getting a solid car.  I love the 300ZX, wish my brother wouldn't have sold his.  He couldnt afford the insurance anymore (i.e. the reason why I won't have one for a while)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||FLASHY||05-14-2001||10:53 PM||||Thanks guys! I checked into insurance for one of those. My wife is already paying $1,700 per year on her '98 Stratus and it would only cost an additional $300 per year to insure a '90-91 300zx (non-turbo). Ok it sounds a little bad because we'd be going down to an older car but look what the trade would be.||||reg||7
